From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:55:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sysprop: generated C++ uses the property API when built for
 Android

CppGen emits SetProp and GetProp with the bionic __system_property_*
path under __BIONIC__ and android::base::Get/SetProperty otherwise.
A device build against another C library that provides the bionic
property API defines __ANDROID__ but not __BIONIC__; the generated
library then needs libbase, which sysprop_library links on host only,
and fails to link. Widen the guards to __BIONIC__ || __ANDROID__. No
change for Soong variants: device builds define both, linux_bionic
defines __BIONIC__.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [no Soong variant defines __ANDROID__ without __BIONIC__]
Patch-Reason: the guards are in code the generator emits, out of reach of the launcher, loader and environment; defining __BIONIC__ instead would change the libc++ ABI on glibc
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 CppGen.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CppGen.cpp b/CppGen.cpp
index 58efde27c0533971355c667fffa80c0d1a2b743b..99b0f5a22ec785bb0be11c8fd63aad96f1ee9ae6 100644
--- a/CppGen.cpp
+++ b/CppGen.cpp
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ constexpr const char* kCppSourceIncludes =
 #include <utility>
 
 #include <strings.h>
-#ifdef __BIONIC__
+#if defined(__BIONIC__) || defined(__ANDROID__)
 #include <sys/system_properties.h>
 [[maybe_unused]] static bool SetProp(const char* key, const char* value) {
     return __system_property_set(key, value) == 0;
@@ -214,7 +214,7 @@ template <typename T>
 template <typename T>
 T GetProp(const char* key, const char* legacy = nullptr) {
     std::string value;
-#ifdef __BIONIC__
+#if defined(__BIONIC__) || defined(__ANDROID__)
     auto pi = __system_property_find(key);
     if (pi != nullptr) {
         __system_property_read_callback(pi, [](void* cookie, const char*, const char* value, std::uint32_t) {
